+# Root-level ESM syntax coverage gap — 2026-09-28
+
+## Task
+Extend the single existing JavaScript syntax gate (`scripts/check-js.js`) so the
+7 root-level `*.mjs` runtime entry points are actually syntax-checked by every
+automated gate, and add a behavioural regression test that proves the gate now
+fails closed on a broken root ESM.
+
+## Why
+Fleet PRE independently falsified PR #320/#326 with finding F3: the gate
+(`npm run check:fast` -> `scripts/check-js.js`) only covers `server.js`,
+`shared/common.js`, `api/*.js`, `lib/*.js` and `apps/*/client.js`. It does not
+cover root-level `*.mjs` — precisely the extension of `telegram-story.mjs`,
+`telegram-state.mjs` and `telegram-game.mjs`, the files those PRs change. A
+candidate can therefore ship a syntactically broken Telegram/Chain Reaction
+runtime entry point while every green check stays green.
+
+This is a release-control defect in a file that open PR #324 does NOT touch, so
+it is owned separately from the Ocean eligibility gate and does not duplicate
+that PR.
+
+## Current state
+Branch `ai/opencode/check-js-root-mjs-coverage-20260928`, created from exact
+current default head `16ef2c6ccdeec6f9888c94ac4d78bcadef1d24cb`
+(`fix: restore free-tier Groq model calls for Chain Reaction and Telegram (#345)`).
+Previous default head / rollback reference: `16ef2c6c`. LKG unchanged: this is a
+CI-only delta with no schema, data, runtime, dependency or deploy change.
+
+## Target state
+One syntax gate covers CommonJS runtime entry points, browser clients and
+root-level ESM entry points. A broken root `*.mjs` fails `npm run check`,
+`npm run check:fast`, quality, godot and fleet-pre, exactly as a broken `lib/*.js`
+already does.
+
+## Files / systems involved
+- `scripts/check-js.js` — the single existing gate; extended, not duplicated.
+- `test/check-js-syntax-coverage.test.js` — new behavioural regression test.
+- `WORK_IN_PROGRESS.md` — this evidence entry.
+
+No new dependency. No new workflow, no parallel gate, no second checker.
+
+## Exact patch / change plan
+1. Extract target discovery and the check loop out of the inline script body
+   into exported functions `collectTargets(rootDir)` and
+   `checkTargets(rootDir, spawn)`, mirroring the existing
+   `scripts/independent-review-gate.cjs` convention of pure exported functions
+   with a thin CLI.
+2. Add root-level `*.mjs` files to the ESM target list, checked through the same
+   `node --check --input-type=module` stdin path already used for
+   `apps/*/client.js`.
+3. Preserve existing behaviour exactly: same child-process flags, same
+   diagnostics, same propagation of the child's exit status, same
+   `Syntax OK: N JavaScript files` summary line, and `main()` still runs on
+   direct execution.
+4. Add a behavioural test that builds a throwaway fixture root in the OS temp
+   directory and runs the real exported checker against it, asserting a broken
+   root `*.mjs` is rejected and a valid one is accepted. The test must not
+   create, mutate or depend on files inside the repository, so it cannot race
+   the parallel `node --test` runner.
+
+## Known risks
+- A currently-valid root `*.mjs` could be rejected by `--input-type=module`.
+  Pre-verified before editing: all 7 files pass the exact invocation, so the
+  change turns no currently-green gate red.
+- `--input-type=module` is a stdin-only flag; root `*.mjs` must use the same
+  stdin path as `apps/*/client.js`, not the `path` argument form.
+- `test/` files run in parallel; any test that writes into the repository root
+  could make an unrelated concurrent `check-js` run fail spuriously. The new
+  test therefore uses a temp fixture root and never the real root.
+
+## Errors that must not return
+- A tautological test that only regex-matches the source text of `check-js.js`.
+- A `check-js` that reports success for a file it never passed to `node --check`.
+- A second, parallel syntax checker, or a new dependency.
+- Weakening, skipping or relaxing any existing gate or test.
+
+## Tests to run
+- `node --test test/check-js-syntax-coverage.test.js`
+- `npm run check:fast`
+- `node scripts/check-js.js`
+- `npm run check`
+- `node scripts/check-agent-rules.js`
+- `npm run golden:check`
+- `git diff --check`
+- Negative reproduction: a deliberately broken root `*.mjs` must now make
+  `node scripts/check-js.js` exit non-zero, then be deleted.
+
+## Deployment / PR plan
+Single PR from `ai/opencode/check-js-root-mjs-coverage-20260928` into `master`.
+No direct master push, no merge, no production deployment. Heavy verification
+is delegated to existing cloud CI. Ocean integration and Fleet POST are
+separate, owner-gated steps and are NOT claimed here.
+
+## Current progress
+Root cause reproduced before editing: with a deliberately broken root
+`zz-repro-syntax-probe.mjs` present, `node scripts/check-js.js` exited 0 with
+"Syntax OK: 67 JavaScript files" while `node --check` on the same file exited 1.
+The probe file was deleted. All 7 real root `*.mjs` files verified to pass the
+exact `--check --input-type=module` stdin invocation. Implementation next.
+
+## Next action
+Implement the `scripts/check-js.js` change, add the behavioural regression
+test, run the gates above, commit, push and open the PR.
+
+## Completion criteria
+A broken root `*.mjs` fails the shared gate; all 7 real root `*.mjs` still pass;
+`npm run check` stays green with no test weakened or skipped; no new dependency,
+workflow or duplicate checker; behaviour covered by an executed test rather
+than a text match.
+
+## Final evidence
+Pending current-run verification.
